  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="1db5-a7ab-dca0-b4d6" name="Sumerian and Akkadian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #103 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Sumer was a collection of city states in Southern Iraq, eventually controlled by a “Lugal” or king. The states waged war against each other and the surrounding peoples. The Akkadians were a distinct group from central Iraq, which rose under Sargon to defeat and subjugate Sumer by 2100 BC and form the first known empire, though it suffered from constant internal revolt and incursions by nomads and the Elamites. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Sumerian and Akkadian]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariots: up to 40%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariots: up to 40% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
